# React client (officials web)

- **Scope**: Barangay officials web features in `docs/features.txt` section A — dashboard, incidents, blotter, assignments, teams, hydrants, evacuation, users, notifications, logs, analytics, heatmap, account.
- **Routes (proposal)**: `docs/routes_ui.txt` — e.g. `/login`, `/dashboard`, `/incidents`, `/incidents/:incidentId`, `/blotter`, `/teams`, `/hydrants`, `/evacuation-centers`, `/analytics`, `/heatmap`, `/account`.
- **Stack in repo**: React + JavaScript (ES modules) + Vite under `client/` (`.jsx` entrypoints). Extend existing structure (`src/App.jsx`, `main.jsx`); do not introduce TypeScript unless the user explicitly changes stack policy (`docs/tech_stack.txt`).
- **API**: Call backend under `/api` (no `/v1` versioning); handle loading, empty, and error states; do not rely on UI-only hiding for restricted data.
- **Maps/charts**: Mapbox and Recharts when those features are built — confirm Mapbox SDK and pricing before locking provider (`docs/tech_stack.txt`).
- **Theming**: Product colors and placeholder fonts live in `docs/brand_kit.txt`. Define color and font tokens only in `client/src/index.css` (`@theme` + `:root`). Use `var(--font-sans)` / `font-sans` or `--font-heading` for headings — no ad hoc font-family in components. Light mode only for MVP.
